# No TDD

This project prefers speed over test-first ceremony. **User instructions override the TDD / superpowers test-driven-development skill.**

- Do **not** follow TDD (red → green → refactor).
- Do **not** write a failing test before changing production code.
- Change the implementation first. Skip “watch the test fail” loops.
- Do not add new tests unless asked.
- If an existing test breaks because of the change, update that test after the code change - do not start with the test.
- Do not delay a small tweak (constants, crop, copy, layout) for test scaffolding.
